        "id": 5020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T20:30:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Encoding only one or two frames won\u0027t exercise much of the encoder. Too many will produce timeouts. Rather than relying on the input data alone to provide random data. It might be better to generate an artificial image. Pure noise or a flat image will also fail to hit various parts of the encoder.\n\nFor frame count selection, a table based on cpu used might be a good choice. We can then refine it based on the fuzzer performance. Something like 50-100 frames to start might be enough.",
      "revId": "87cc63b4d814aeaadf2b88ceff2e197e3c20badb",
